@@ -138,3 +138,7 @@ Validate fusion on held-out shapes before promotion: [stage28 BF16 shape checks]
 For BI-V150 SwiGLU, retain the default compiled native baseline and distinguish the new17.9M gated model from earlier13.7M GELU trials; read [stage29](sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage29.md) and [the activation page](wiki/kernels/swiglu-megatron-bi-v150.md). Compiler/controller failures, numerical rejection and training regressions remain separate evidence; never infer throughput for an unmeasured candidate.
 
 For BI-V150 heldout SwiGLU and native fused Attention, read [stage30](sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage30.md) and [stage31](sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage31.md). Stage30 retains its inherited softmax fusionFalse contract; stage31 proves and retains native default fusionTrue. Compare only fresh same-round controls and reject broken audit metadata even when timing appears faster.
+
+### Stage32: larger-model Attention validation
+
+Read [stage32](sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage32.md) before reusing Attention003 on larger BF16 models. It restores native compiled SwiGLU and default fused causal softmax; compare each same-round control, and enforce all-seed promotion instead of averaging away a regression.
