 ### Stages30/31: heldout models and native fused Attention
 
 Keep each model/backend contract distinct: stage30 fixed SwiGLU004 heldout validation has inherited softmax fusionFalse, stage31 full Attention uses proved native default fusionTrue. Preserve BF16 stage boundaries, native GEMMs/Softmax, all gradients and FP32 masters. SDPA availability does not establish numerical compatibility; broken audit metadata invalidates formal throughput claims. [Stage30](../sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage30.md) and [stage31](../sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage31.md).
+
+### Stage32: larger-model Attention validation
+
+Read [stage32](../sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage32.md) before reusing Attention003 on larger BF16 models. It restores native compiled SwiGLU and default fused causal softmax; compare each same-round control, and enforce all-seed promotion instead of averaging away a regression.
